    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10765" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντονομ-ασία</span></b> , ἡ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>use of an epithet,
				patronymic,</i> or <i>appellative for a proper name,</i> and
			vice versa, <i><span class="en">
				Trypho
				<u>Trop.</u>
				2.17
			</span></i>, Ps.-<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
			</span></i><i>Vita Hom.</i><i><span class="en">
				24
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. καὶ μετάληψις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Demetr.Lac.
					<u>Herc.</u>
					1014.19
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				20
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>nomination of his successor by retiring official,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				POxy.
				1642.15
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A.D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> Gramm., 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντωνυμία</span>
			, <i>pronoun,</i> or <i>the use of it,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Comp.</u>
				2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Pron.</u>
				4.18
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> Arith.,
				<i>contrary denomination,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Nicom.
				<u>Ar.</u>
				1.23
			</span></i>.</div>
